{
  "id": 340955221,
  "iid": 17965,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "DNP3: Only add reassembled AL packets in the FINAL fragment",
  "description": "It's possible to have multiple DNP3 AL fragments in the same\nTCP segment. (or UDP datagram?)\n\nInstead of checking the packet number and layer number (the last\nof which is not useful, as tcp_dissect_pdus doesn't increase the\nlayer number for each pdu), simply check if the Final bit is set.\nThis prevents adding the reassembled packet multiple times in such\ncases. (HTTP/2 has a similar approach.)\n\nAlso, if this isn't the first Data Link segment (PDU) then add a\nseparator when adding additional DNP3 transport information to\nthe Info column.\n\nFix #14436",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-11-06T11:06:38.944Z",
